+// A simple approach: iterate over input logical elements; for each, compute multi-dimensional index,
+// then compute mask index using mask strides and shape (broadcast).
+
+// This is easier if we have input_shape and mask_shape/strides.
+// We'll implement a kernel that loops over input elements (grid-stride) and for each:
+//   1. compute multi-index from linear index and input_shape.
+//   2. compute mask_index using mask_strides and mask_shape with broadcasting (if mask dim smaller, align trailing and skip leading).
+//   3. if mask[mask_index] is true, selected.
+// This is O(N) computational overhead but safe and parallel-friendly.
+
